# Model Card: cardsort-base-v2

## Overview

cardsort-base-v2 is a text classification model that routes short support
messages into one of eight intent categories. It is trained on internal
support transcripts and evaluated on a held out split from the same source.

## Intended Use

The model is intended for triage of inbound support messages in English. It
should not be used as the sole decision maker for account actions.

## Capabilities

- claim: Classifies the eight supported intents with accuracy above 0.90 on the held out split. (cites: eval-intent-accuracy)
- claim: Keeps median response latency under 40 milliseconds on the reference CPU. (cites: eval-latency-median)
- claim: Maintains macro F1 above 0.85 across all eight classes. (cites: eval-macro-f1)
- claim: Supports a new escalation intent bringing the total to nine classes. (cites: eval-escalation-recall)

## Limitations

- Trained only on English transcripts, so non English input is out of scope.
- Accuracy drops on messages longer than 512 tokens because they are truncated.
- Latency figures assume a warm process and do not include cold start cost.

## Results

eval-intent-accuracy = accuracy 0.91
eval-latency-median = latency_ms 37
eval-macro-f1 = macro_f1 0.87
eval-refund-billing-confusion = confusion_rate 0.14
eval-escalation-recall = recall 0.82

